// DF-172f: one rule, two positions, and until design 172 part 2 only one of
// them had a diagnostic. `[T; N]`'s length is fixed at compile time, so a
// module `static` in that position is refused — but the REPEAT literal
// (`[0; ARENA_BYTES]`) said so cleanly while the TYPE annotation
// (`[UInt8; ARENA_BYTES]`) reached codegen with an unresolved length and died
// as `internal compiler error: Array type missing element type or size`.
//
// Design 148 already named this position as the one that owns the requirement
// ("a declared array length reaching codegen reports it"); it just raised the
// wrong kind of error. Found writing the SOS arena, whose size wants ONE
// spelling — the working one is a named array type plus `sizeof`.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: array length is not a compile-time constant
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: `ARENA_BYTES`

static ARENA_BYTES: Int = 1024

static ARENA: [UInt8; ARENA_BYTES] = [0; 1024]

func main() {
    print(ARENA[0])
}
